  $ \( n + 1 \) t k_0 N gt.eq n t \( p - 1 \) . $
  Thus these products span the thick point defined by the $p$-th powers of all $n t$ smooth parameters. This is the elementary comparison of ordinary and Frobenius jets used in [31] Proposition 2.12. Etaleness identifies the completed local rings at the torsor lift and its tuple in $W^t$, and therefore identifies these thick points.
  For an $N$-fold product of pure tensors, write $m'_i$ for the new exponent in slot $i$. Then $0 lt.eq m'_i lt.eq N \( r - 1 \) < p r$ and $sum_i m'_i equiv 0 med \( mod med r \)$. Choose $a_i$ in $\[ r \, 2 r - 1 \]$ with $p a_i equiv m'_i med \( mod med r \)$. Their sum is a multiple of $r$ less than $q = 2 t r$. Increase $a_1$ by the difference to obtain
  $ a_i gt.eq 0 \, #h(2em) sum_i a_i = q \, #h(2em) p a_i gt.eq m'_i . $
